course: dictionary
lesson: 7909
title: One word, several meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one to use. «Ratings are decided by trained examiners who follow published rules.» Here a rating is a judgement, not a row of numbers.
explain: Look at the clues around the word. In «a five-star rating», the stars show it is a score for how good something is. In «parental controls that can block games above a chosen age rating», the word age tells you a rating can be a label for which ages something suits.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. If «a high rating» still makes sense with your meaning, you have probably chosen the right one. If it sounds silly, look for other clues in the text.
fact: Rating means a score, grade or label that shows how good, popular or safe something is.
fact: A rating can also be an age label, such as the one on a film or game that shows which ages it suits.
fact: In TV, ratings are numbers showing how many people watched a programme.
fact: Useful phrases: age rating, star rating, high rating, low rating, and rating of 4 out of 5.
fact: Families use age ratings to choose before they press play, so check the rating first.
exercise: «Ratings are decided by trained examiners who follow published rules.» Who decides the rating? | The film makers | The shop that sells the film | Anyone who makes a guess | *Trained examiners who follow published rules
exercise: «The shop has a rating of 4 out of 5 stars.» What does rating mean here? | A film about the shop | A label saying which ages can visit | A count of the people who watched | *A score showing how good the shop is
exercise: Which sentence uses rating to mean an age label? | «A credit score is a rating of how reliably someone pays.» | «My best rating is in maths.» | *«Parental controls can block games above a chosen age rating.» | «Fire danger rating signs show how dangerous a fire would be.»
test: «A credit score is a rating of how reliably someone pays; missing payments lowers it.» What does a lower rating show? | That the score is a long word | That someone is famous | That someone pays very reliably | *That someone has missed payments and is less reliable
test: Which of these is a rating that shows how dangerous a fire would be? | Ratings from a TV show | Five-star rating on an app | Age rating on a game | *Fire danger rating sign
exam: Pick the best meaning of «a high rating» for a shopping app. | *Customers scored it well | It is the tallest building in town | The app runs very slowly | It costs the most money
